# A rule ending in `/` matches a directory and NOT a symlink of the same name,
# so each relocatable directory below is listed twice, with and without the
# slash. Without the slashless form, moving a full directory to another disk and
# symlinking it back leaves every byte of it committable with no warning. That
# is not hypothetical: it put an absolute machine path into a commit in the
# sibling repository. Verify a change here with `git status --porcelain
# --untracked-files=all`, not by reading the rule, and not with `git
# check-ignore -q`, which exits 0 on a negation match too.
#
# `real_trials` is deliberately NOT listed slashless. A bare rule would match
# the directory and git cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory,
# which would kill the negations that track trials.csv and the sheets.
*.pyc
*.txt
*.egg-info/
*.egg-info/*
output_dump/
output_dump
*.mp4
*.pdf
.claude/
/.worktrees/
recordings/
recordings
/calibration/
/calibration
/chassis_calibration/
/chassis_calibration
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Planner output artifacts under real_test_envs/<env>/solution/.
# These are produced by `run_namo.py --sim-xml` runs (per-run plan dirs +
# driver-level logs). Treat the canonical scene/pose files at the env root
# as the committed inputs; planner outputs are reproducible from them.
/real_test_envs/**/solution/random_rollout/
/real_test_envs/**/solution/random_rollout_run*_driver.log

# Closed-loop experiment sessions are large local outputs. This covers the
# standard workspace and named variants such as less-depth or execution roots.
/closed_loop_sessions*/*
!/closed_loop_sessions/README.md

# Local verification scratch space.
/_tmp_real_test_envs_verify/
build_cards/
build_cards

# real_trials/ holds two different kinds of thing and they need opposite
# treatment. trials.csv is the study's record of record and sheets_v2_*/ are
# the analysis inputs the pre-registration names by path; a result nobody else
# can read is not reproducible, so both belong in git. Everything else under it
# is generated bulk: videos, the raw push archive, per-subgoal jsonl, run logs.
#
# Exclude the CONTENTS rather than the directory. `real_trials/` excludes the
# directory itself and git will not re-include a path under an excluded
# directory, so the negations below would never fire.
real_trials/*
!real_trials/trials.csv
!real_trials/sheets_v2_*/

# The compiled binding lives in namo_cpp, but a worktree here has none of its
# own and symlinking the main tree's build in is the obvious move. No rule
# existed at all, so that symlink was untracked and stageable.
build_python/
build_python
